From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0923 redfin: /dev/redwood-camera, the cameras' frames for iOS

Boot-arg sweetcamdev=1 (with sweetcam=2): HackiOS redwood_camera.c's cam=5
device (sys/redwood_camera.h: read a frame header + RAW10, write EXPOSURE /
SENSOR / FOCUS commands) for its userland camera_device.c in mediaserverd.
A session from the first read to the last close (or a second without a
read, or a fault): the sensor brought up by stream_up() (the bring-up of
"c 21", split out of capture_sensor()), three places of GPU-pool memory
below 4 GB, write-combined, the write master given the next place's address
at each RDI 0 start of frame, the exposure written in the sensor's group
hold between frames. Sensors as HackiOS numbers them: 1 back = IMX363,
2 front = IMX355, 3 ultra-wide = IMX481 (sweetcam_sensor= picks the first,
sweetcam_mode= its mode; else the most pixels at 4:3, <= 31 fps, <= 13 MP).
Gain is linear for the program (256 = 1x; IMX363 up to 8x, the others 16x),
the Sony code (512 - 512/g, 1024 - 1024/g) for the sensor. No lens motor
yet: FOCUS is taken and ignored. "c 20/21" are refused while it streams;
the stage names of "c 22" are off unless asked for. r18a: camera_test
reads frames with AE; the places are cached now (uncached they copied at
~120 MB/s), the frame's lines forgotten before each copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WuzsiVGCDDmN2GPRLJvX3w
